  "final_message": "The key is **`AUD-ORDER-7781`**.\n\n1. `service.checkout(\"7781\")` calls `write_audit(\"order\", \"7781\")` in `audit.py`.\n2. `audit.py` builds keys with `_format_key`, which returns `f\"{AUDIT_PREFIX}-{kind.upper()}-{ident}\"`. `AUDIT_PREFIX` is `\"AUD\"` in `config.py`, so the result is `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n3. My tool output hid the actual key-assignment line in `write_audit` (it showed as `[REDACTED:SECRET]`), so I couldn't read it directly. Instead I ran `write_audit('order', '7781')`, which is the same call `checkout(\"7781\")` makes. The only key in the log was `['AUD-ORDER-7781']`.\n\n`decoy_metrics.py` builds keys starting with `MET-` and `decoy_cache.py` is a plain cache. Neither writes to the audit log.\n\nANSWER: AUD-ORDER-7781",
